  "answers": {
    "netmedex_hybrid_rag": "**Direct evidence for hop 1 – dysbiosis → periodontitis**  \nHuman metatranscriptomic data from sub‑gingival plaque of progressing sites show that shifts in the relative abundance of oral microbes create a dysbiotic community that precedes clinical periodontitis and inflammation【PMID:25918553】 (human).\n\n**Direct evidence for hop 2 – periodontitis → bone loss**  \nHuman studies describe periodontitis as a disease linked to dysbiosis in which the accumulated oral pathobionts provoke immune responses that “promote alveolar bone loss” around teeth【PMID:24646638】 (human).\n\n**Overall mechanistic inference**  \nThe two pieces of direct evidence together support a mechanistic chain (dysbiosis → periodontitis → bone loss). No single study in the supplied set demonstrates the complete three‑step causal sequence; the inference is built by linking the separate hop‑wise findings.\n\n### Graph‑derived candidate insights\n- **PATH 5724030babeb80f1 GRAPH‑CONFIRMED**: dysbiosis *leads_to* periodontitis *associated_with* bone loss | PMIDs 25918553, 24646638 | human evidence (GRAPH‑CONFIRMED).  \n\n**Conclusion:** Human data substantiate each individual hop—microbial dysbiosis initiating periodontitis and periodontitis driving alveolar bone loss—forming a coherent mechanistic pathway, as confirmed by the graph."
  },
